-- R2 — the test-body exemption, deliberate and scoped (2026-08-05).
--
-- `test` and `describe` bodies have no `main`, so there is nowhere for a
-- capability to be granted from. Without an exemption, capability behaviour
-- would not be testable from March at all.
--
-- So `root_cap` stays nameable HERE and nowhere else (reject/t152 is the
-- counterpart). This is a real remaining hole and is documented as one: it is
-- ambient authority, scoped to a context that cannot reach production code —
-- a dependency's `test` blocks do not run in a consumer's build.
--
-- The exemption is enforced by checking the enclosing context, not by the
-- checker simply failing to look. If it were the latter, this file would pass
-- for the wrong reason and reject/t152 would be the only thing standing
-- between the language and its old behaviour.
mod TestBodyCaps do
  needs IO

  describe "capabilities are reachable from a test body" do
    test "narrowing the root inside a test" do
      let console : Cap(IO.Console) = cap_narrow(root_cap)
      assert(true)
    end
  end
end
